&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employer&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Block, Inc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Intercompany and Global Structuring Lead&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Location&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Oakland, CA&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Duties &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee Block&#39;s global intercompany and transfer pricing policies, including: (i) quarterly intercompany calculations and required journal entries; (ii) global transfer pricing documentation obligations, (iii) monitoring global intercompany relationships with a view to identify activities that require a new agreement or revisions to existing agreements; and (iv) working with Counsel and other stakeholder teams to draft and execute such agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and resolve global transfer pricing risks and controversy matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute across all U.S. international, cross-border, and non-U.S. tax matters impacting Block&#39;s business, including: (i) advising on the tax consequences and planning of projects and operating strategies, such as expansion into new markets and the launches of new products; (ii) help integrate newly acquired companies; (iii) help with the implementation of tax strategies; (iv) provide support with Block&#39;s quarterly tax rate, tax forecasts close process, and annual U.S. international tax compliance requirements; (v) tax modeling, research, and planning for U.S. international tax matters (GILTI, FDII, FTC, BEAT, etc.) and foreign tax matters (CIT, VAT, WHT); and (vi) developing correspondence regarding tax audits and examinations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Global Tax Advisory team in the development, feasibility analysis, and implementation of new tax strategies and plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and rationalize Block’s legal entity structure through mergers, dissolutions, and liquidations, ensuring operational efficiency and cost savings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct tax research related to different Block products in different countries, draft memoranda, and other written documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate knowledge of past, present, and potential future international tax laws, guidance, and court decisions that are applicable to the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform the quarterly close process, including contributions to the required tax provision memoranda.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead tax support on Global Mobility matters, hiring, short-term international work, and other jurisdictional issues related to people matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
